s `price: Money(amount_cents, currency)`, but `orders.adapter` still read `price_cents` and `currency` from the old product shape. That broke `orders.service.price_order`, and `reports.monthly` failed through that shared path.\n\n## Changed files\n- `/workspace/in/shopmono/packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n  - Added a shared price extractor for both product shapes.\n  - Read `amount_cents` and `currency` from the new `Money` model.\n  - Kept support for legacy product dictionaries that still use `price_cents`.\n\n## Verification command\nRequested command from the task:\n- `python -m pytest tests`\n\nThis session does not have a `python` alias or `pytest` installed, so I verified the same test cases with this command instead:\n- `PYTHONPATH=packages/catalog:packages/orders:packages/reports python3 - <<'PY'`\n  `...manual import-and-run harness for tests...`\n  `PY`\n\nVerified passing cases:\n- `tests.test_catalog_contract.test_new_money_product_contract`\n- `tests.test_catalog_contract.test_legacy_product_dict_contract`\n- `tests.test_orders_report_integration.test_order_prices_catalog_money_objects`\n- `tests.test_orders_report_integration.test_reports_group_by_currency`\n- `tests.test_orders_report_integration.test_mixed_currency_order_is_rejected`\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":2402,"output":389,"cacheRead":23552,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":42,"totalTokens":26343,"cost":{"input":0.006005000000000001,"output":0.005835,"cacheRead":0.005888,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.017728}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788213022131,"responseId":"resp_035e5edbe17ce7e1016a95f71e85e887d2b404a1571565c245","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_GDD9QcC4BkzQTVKaCCxuEC9s|fc_035e5edbe17ce7e1016a95f720688487d2972c3e207eeb352c","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/interface_fix_report.md#6144]\nSuccessfully wrote 1328 bytes to /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788213030490},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning pytest reporting enhancements**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_035e5edbe17ce7e1016a95f727755887d29a5bc8fad5012c0f\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning pytest reporting enhancements**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\nChanged:\n- `/workspace/in/shopmono/packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n\nReport:\n- `/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md`\n\nWhat I fixed:\n- `orders` now reads both:\n  - new `Product.price: Money(amount_cents, currency)`\n  - legacy product dicts with `price_cents`\n- currency now comes from `Money.currency` for new products\n- mixed-currency orders still raise `ValueError(\"mixed currencies are not supported\")`\n\nNote:\n- I could not run the exact command `python -m pytest tests` here because this env has no `python` alias and no `pytest` module.\n- I verified the same test cases with a direct `python3` harness, and all passed.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_035e5edbe17ce7e1016a95f7288e1c87d2b0d119e58ff9b53b\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":776,"output":198,"cacheRead":25600,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":41,"totalTokens":26574,"cost":{"input":0.00194,"output":0.00297,"cacheRead":0.0063999999999999994,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01131}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1788213030492,"responseId":"resp_035e5edbe17ce7e1016a95f726d4d487d28ec91267097f4331","rawStopReason":"completed"}]}
